# 📊 WasteWise: Analytics Dashboard & System Cleanup Walkthrough

This walkthrough outlines the design, implementation, and successful testing of the **Analytics Dashboard** and the **System Cleanup & Refactoring** module for the *WasteWise Smart Urban Waste Collection and Processing Optimization System*. 

---

## 🌟 Executive Summary & Accomplishments
All feature objectives and structural refactoring requirements have been fully implemented, verified, and compiled. Key milestones include:
1. **Clean Modular Architecture**: Restructured the monolithic draft into 10 cohesive packages, successfully decoupling imports and resolving dynamic path lookups for Linux compatibility.
2. **Centralized Operations & Metrics**: Created unified central constants, a robust dynamic logger, and automated CSV helpers, eliminating redundant files and circular references.
3. **Automated Environmental Failover**: Added real-time processing emissions tracking in the `Facility` model and automated failover routing logic to redirect collections to the next best active unit if threshold limits are exceeded.
4. **Interactive Tkinter/Matplotlib Dashboard**: Engineered 5 operational tabs loaded with premium operational KPIs, scrolling event logs, and real-time updating bar, line, and pie charts.

---

## 📂 Reorganized Modular Folder Structure

The project has been cleaned and reorganized into the following package structure under `src/`:

```
src/
├── analytics/
│   └── dashboard.py           # Dashboard calculations, layouts, and Matplotlib chart helpers
├── auth/
│   ├── auth.py                # Session authentication and login history logger
│   ├── user.py                # Core User data model
│   └── user_manager.py        # Resident registry and DB management
├── data/
│   ├── users.csv              # Resident profiles database
│   ├── login_history.csv      # Session history database
│   ├── disposal_events.csv    # Live resident waste disposal logs
│   ├── emergency_logs.csv     # Dynamic critical incident records
│   ├── route_logs.csv         # Fleet optimized route statistics
│   ├── facility_logs.csv      # Facility events and failovers
│   └── waste_mapping.json     # Standard Composition and zone boundaries
├── emergency/
│   └── emergency_handler.py   # Critical overflow rules and incident management
├── facilities/
│   └── facility_allocation.py # Route-to-processing allocation & automated failover
├── gui/
│   └── gui.py                 # Premium Tkinter User Interface
├── models/
│   └── models.py              # Base data objects (Bin, Vehicle, Facility)
├── routing/
│   ├── distance_graph.py      # Dijkstra city routing graph
│   └── route_optimizer.py     # Multi-bin heuristic route optimizer
├── simulation/
│   ├── data_loader.py         # Sample data loader for city nodes
│   ├── engine.py              # Central simulation lifecycle orchestrator
│   ├── monitoring.py          # Real-time bin capacity tracking
│   ├── priority.py            # Urgency priority scoring engine
│   ├── vehicle_allocation.py  # Fleet dispatch allocation
│   └── input_processor.py     # User disposal contamination assessment
├── utils/
│   ├── constants.py           # Standard weights, limits, multipliers, and theme colors
│   ├── csv_utils.py           # Dynamic, directory-safe CSV CRUD handlers
│   └── logger.py              # Centralized logging module with unified timestamps
├── gui.py                     # Backward-compatible GUI Entry Point Launcher
└── main.py                    # Backward-compatible CLI Entry Point Launcher
```

> [!NOTE]
> All legacy monolithic files (including the old `user_management` directory) have been cleanly removed, and redundant logic was successfully unified into reusable helpers.

